1. Client Section – Transaction Filter Issue

In the Client section, when applying the Last 30 Days filter under Transactions, only Karvy transactions are being displayed.
Please investigate and fix the issue so that all transactions within the selected date range are displayed.
Also, provide an option to select a custom date range using “From” and “To” filters.

2. All Transactions – Date Filter Issue

In the All Transactions section, when selecting a date range such as Last 14–15 Days, only one transaction is being displayed.
However, a KFintech transaction that occurred yesterday is not appearing in the list.
Please investigate and ensure that all transactions falling within the selected date range are displayed correctly.

3. BSE Auto File Fetch – Auto Fetch Setting Not Being Followed

BSE Auto is fetching the files again after some time, even though the files already exist.
Since the files are already available, the system is skipping them, but the auto-fetch process is still getting triggered.
As per the database, the auto-fetch setting is turned OFF, but the system is not following this configuration.
Please investigate why the database setting is not being respected and ensure that the auto-fetch process follows the configured ON/OFF status.

4. Separate Daily NAV Download

The Daily NAV download process needs to be separated from the existing auto-fetch functionality.
Daily NAV downloading should have its own dedicated process/configuration so that it can be managed independently.

5. NAV Auto-Fetch Logic

For the remaining NAV auto-fetch functionality, we can keep the existing automated process.
The system should automatically fetch NAV files only when the previous day's NAV or the required NAV for the last 7 days is not available.
Before initiating a download, the system should check whether the required NAV data/file already exists.
If the NAV is already available, the system should skip the download and avoid unnecessary fetching.